# Agent/session tooling artifacts (local-only; never versioned).
# Also keeps Codex headless review payloads under its 1 MiB input limit — these
# dirs were being inlined into the council adversarial-review prompt and
# tripping "Input exceeds maximum length".
.council/
.cursor/
.firecrawl/
.superpowers/
.understand-anything/
.vite/
docs/handoffs/
# graphify-out/ is versioned here (fork/local-main only — Recipe A in
# FORK-WORKFLOW.md keeps it out of upstream PRs by branch discipline, not by
# gitignore). Overrides the machine-wide default in ~/.config/git/ignore and
# this repo's own .git/info/exclude, both of which still ignore it globally.
# Anchored to the repo root only — per-subfolder graphify-out/ dirs (e.g. from
# a multi-subfolder `graphify extract`) stay ignored as merge intermediates by
# the unanchored rules in ~/.config/git/ignore and .git/info/exclude. Do NOT add
# a bare `graphify-out/` here to enforce that: unanchored and later in the file,
# it would also re-ignore the root tree this negation exists to version.
!/graphify-out/
/graphify-out/cost.json
# Regenerable scratch inside graphify-out/ — never worth versioning.
# (gitignore has no inline-comment syntax: a trailing "# ..." is part of the
# pattern, not a comment — each rule gets its own comment line above it.)
# AST extraction cache, rebuilt by any `graphify extract`:
/graphify-out/cache/
# Dated backups written by cluster-only/label before overwrite:
/graphify-out/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]/
# Machine-local interpreter path, breaks on another machine/CI:
/graphify-out/.graphify_python
# Intermediate; the full skill pipeline (Step 9) deletes it itself:
/graphify-out/.graphify_analysis.json
# Local-only: codebase-memory-mcp team graph artifact (regenerable by re-indexing)
.codebase-memory/
Music/
.npmrc

# docs/superpowers/ is deliberately absent from this file — no ignore rule, and
# therefore no negation either. Plans and specs are this Beta's decision history
# and are versioned on fork/local-main. Nothing outside this repo ignores them
# ("docs/ — NOTHING under it is excluded any more" in .git/info/exclude), so a
# rule + `!` negation pair would only be an ordering trap: the pair used to sit
# here, a third rule far below re-ignored the tree, and `git add` needed -f.
# What keeps this off upstream is NOT this file: it is .git/hooks/pre-push
# (fail-closed on local-only paths) plus FORK-WORKFLOW.md Recipe A. Versioning
# and shipping are separate concerns.
# NOTE: this leaves ~4.6 MB inlined into any tool that reads the working tree.
# If /council-pr trips "Input exceeds maximum length" again, fix it in the
# council's file selection, not by re-ignoring this tree.

# >>> dev-council ephemerals (managed by /council-init — do not edit) >>>
.council/project-map.md
.council/current-plan.md
.council/current-pr-diff.md
.council/peer-prompt-*
.council/round-*
.council/council-result*
.council/debug-*
.council/claude-to-*
.council/adversarial-focus*
.council/cursor-findings*
.council/codex-findings*
.council/deduped-findings*
.council/dedupe-diagnostics.json
.council/delegate-*
.council/repomix-snapshot.md
.council/.cursor-*
.council/.codex-*
.council/.test-cache
.council/.*-status.json
.council/.*-stderr.log
# <<< dev-council ephemerals <<<

# Nothing below this point. A bare `graphify-out/` or `docs/superpowers/` added
# here would silently override the rules above — a later rule wins, so it would
# re-ignore both deliberately-versioned trees and make new files vanish from
# `git status` without any error. Both already have their entry above; add new
# exclusions next to the tree they belong to, not at the end of the file.
